in full and does not contain the Best Reviewed title.

--- 3. The data and the endpoint are both healthy in zone 2 ---
DB (read-only SELECT) — reviewed, active module-2 items per zone:
  zone_id  items_with_reviews
  1        30
  2        30

App network log (adb logcat -s flutter), zone 2 session:
  08-15 23:31:31.213 I flutter : [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/items/most-reviewed
  08-15 23:31:40.118 I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/items/most-reviewed http_status=200
  08-15 23:32:10.229 I flutter : [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/items/most-reviewed
  08-15 23:32:30.920 I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/items/most-reviewed http_status=200

Direct API check (read-only GET, both zones return a populated payload):
  zoneId [1] moduleId 2 -> {"total_size":30, ... "products":[{"id":118,"name":"French Fries" ...
  zoneId [2] moduleId 2 -> {"total_size":30, ... "products":[{"id":542,"name":"Chicago Style Cheese" ...

So: data exists, endpoint returns 200 with 30 products, yet the rail does not mount
in zone 2. Mechanism NOT identified — needs triage. No [FAIL]/[ERR] line was emitted
(0 error-class lines in 359 flutter log lines for the whole session), so if this is a
swallowed empty/error path it is also a logging-contract gap.

Severity: medium (a whole merchandising rail silently missing for every zone-2
customer). Not a blocker for NEARS-1934 — filed as a separate pre-existing defect.
